            "body": "Same state in, same reference out. That's the selector contract.\n\nuseSelector compares with ===. A selector returning { ...todo, todoItems } creates a new object every call — 3 theme toggles = 3 wasted re-renders.\n\nshallowEqual helps on 'All' but fails on 'Active' because filter() makes a new array.\n\ncreateSelector over stable inputs takes it to zero re-renders.\n\nOne test locks it in: change an unrelated slice, expect the same reference back. toBe, not toEqual.\n\nBuild it yourself on Elegant. Free, no sign-up. Link in description.\n\n#frontend #redux #javascript #reactjs #webdev #shorts"
