              "duration_seconds": 60,
              "thumbnail": "assets/thumbnails/state-pairs.jpg"
            },
            "body": "useState vs useReducer — they sound similar, work differently.\n\nuseState: independent values, simple updates.\nuseReducer: updates depend on previous state, or multiple sub-values change together.\n\nThe boundary: if your setter calls the previous state, or you're updating { loading: true, data: [], error: null } all at once — that's useReducer territory.\n\nWe mapped 5 state pairs in our glossary. This is pair #1.\n\nPractice the decision on Elegant. Free, no sign-up. Link in description.\n\n#frontend #react #state #javascript #webdev #shorts"
          },
